{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511501-antediluvian-blood-properties","id":1511501,"title":"Antediluvian blood properties","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-12T19:15:41-07:00","id":1511501,"title":"Antediluvian blood properties","content":"So, as you probably know already, there are some stated &quot;miraculous&quot; effects of drinking the blood of some beings, among them, perhaps the Antediluvian ones are the most potent. As stated in books published, we only have Malkav's blood and Tremere's blood. Just for fun, giving that a single drop from Malkav's blood is stated to heal all wounds and derangements (save for the <i>permanent</i> one of the Malkavians), increase willpower by 1 and drop the generation by one, what do you guys think drinking the blood of each of the Antediluvians effect would be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-12T23:38:07-07:00","id":1511508,"title":"","content":"I think their blood must be an unstable thing and very likely to go wrong, something like high risk not so high reward. And how does Malkav's blood cure derangements? If even the blood of a thirteenth generation Malkav can drive insanity, Malkav's should break one's mind completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T00:01:55-07:00","id":1511512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511501-antediluvian-blood-properties?p=1511508#post1511508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think their blood must be an unstable thing and very likely to go wrong, something like high risk not so high reward. And how does Malkav's blood cure derangements? If even the blood of a thirteenth generation Malkav can drive insanity, Malkav's should break one's mind completely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Malkav's blood has the effects I mentioned in the text. A single drop heals all wounds and cures all derangements (except for the <b>permanent </b>one of Malkavians), drop generation by 1 and increases <i>permanent</i> Willpower by 1. It's in the story <b>Fountains of Bright Crimson</b>, not sure if you read this supplement for <b>Jerusalem by Night</b>. I was thinking about possible effects for other Antediluvians as a fun exercise, as the only one confirmed canonically is Malkav's (and Tremere's in a way).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T00:23:26-07:00","id":1511516,"title":"","content":"The blood of the Eldest contained the essence of the Tzimsice antediluvian (like the Carnage symbiote bonded with the blood if the sociopathic serial-killer Cletus Kasady) an became basically inpossible to destroy, able to reform from nothing (well a drop of blood) and manifest itself in anyone who tasted Tzimisce blood... ever - not to mention the vicissitude poisoning<br /> <br /> The True Vessel was the semi-legendary recipient of the vitae and soul of the Cappadocian Antediluvian, which would enable Augustus Giovanni to complete the diablerie of his sire.<br /> Aside that, and Japeth used it to Embrace Agustus, the jar was filled with the vitae of Cappadocius for the Embrace ceremony (and Lamia cursed it with the painfull kiss)<br /> So the vitae left in it not only would allow Augustus to complete the diableire, but probably would have other funny properities<br /> <br /> V5 have &quot;Blood of Zapathasura&quot; - Thick,<b> sentient </b>ropes of his vitae stained the ground in Bangladesh where he fell. The noonday sun did not destroy it all. You own a small vial containing the Blood of the Ravnos Antediluvian. What you do with this vitae is up to you, and what it does to anyone who imbibes it is up to the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> The Ventrue Antediluvian had a jar filled with Caine's vitae in his stronghold according the Clanbook<br /> (In a Gehenna scenario the vial with Caine's vitae mad you explode, and allowed Saulot to chanel God wrath and destroy the vampire race)\u200b<br /> <br /> Thesere are the canon ones aside Malkav<br /> I think the blood of an antediluvian would be a huge deal (just think of the possibilites via Quietus or Blood Sorcery) but probably would give you disciplines similar to the Ancient, make your blood thicker (like Malkav's) and strenghten the Curse of the Clan, instead curing it (Malkav barking the rules, because he is Malkav as it was mentioned in Fountains)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 05-13-2023, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T01:08:01-07:00","id":1511519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511501-antediluvian-blood-properties?p=1511516#post1511516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The blood of the Eldest contained the essence of the Tzimsice antediluvian (like the Carnage symbiote bonded with the blood if the sociopathic serial-killer Cletus Kasady) an became basically inpossible to destroy, able to reform from nothing (well a drop of blood) and manifest itself in anyone who tasted Tzimisce blood... ever - not to mention the vicissitude poisoning<br /> <br /> The True Vessel was the semi-legendary recipient of the vitae and soul of the Cappadocian Antediluvian, which would enable Augustus Giovanni to complete the diablerie of his sire.<br /> Aside that, and Japeth used it to Embrace Agustus, the jar was filled with the vitae of Cappadocius for the Embrace ceremony (and Lamia cursed it with the painfull kiss)<br /> So the vitae left in it not only would allow Augustus to complete the diableire, but probably would have other funny properities<br /> <br /> V5 have &quot;Blood of Zapathasura&quot; - Thick,<b> sentient </b>ropes of his vitae stained the ground in Bangladesh where he fell. The noonday sun did not destroy it all. You own a small vial containing the Blood of the Ravnos Antediluvian. What you do with this vitae is up to you, and what it does to anyone who imbibes it is up to the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> The Ventrue Antediluvian had a jar filled with Caine's vitae in his stronghold according the Clanbook<br /> (In a Gehenna scenario the vial with Caine's vitae mad you explode, and allowed Saulot to chanel God wrath and destroy the vampire race)\u200b<br /> <br /> Thesere are the canon ones aside Malkav<br /> I think the blood of an antediluvian would be a huge deal (just think of the possibilites via Quietus or Blood Sorcery) but probably would give you disciplines similar to the Ancient, make your blood thicker (like Malkav's) and strenghten the Curse of the Clan, instead curing it (Malkav barking the rules, because he is Malkav as it was mentioned in Fountains)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, when I said &quot;the only one stated&quot;, I was thinking about giving details of its effects, from what I remember only Malkav's had the effects listed systematically, so to speak. Tremere is possible to infer because of the ritual Invulnerability to Weakness.<br /> <br /> Of the ones you mentioned the one thing I didn't remember was this &quot;jar filled with Caine's blood&quot; (in which clanbook was it? Revised?) and V5 &quot;Blood of Zapathasura&quot; I have no idea where to find.<br /> <br /> And yes, Malkav's breaks the rules lol, his couldn't be predictable, I guess. I think all of them should have as <b>basis</b> the property to drop the generation, give disciplines and increase Willpower. Then I agree that it would be cool if they also made the curse stronger. Still, it's nice to think of different things, like the weird property of Malkav's blood curing derangements, oh and let's not forget healing all wounds is also property thing I think they all should have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T04:06:08-07:00","id":1511532,"title":"","content":"Te 1st ed Ventrue Clanbook, where it talks about the <b>Secret Masters </b>and after discussing them with Caine, the Antediluvian became so scared of them, he turned his palace in the City in to a fortified fortress and gathered all the artifacts he could find, like the Claw of Fenris, the Rainbow Bridge, head of Medusa, and such things, and deep within the fortress he kept a jar with Caine's blood<br /> As for the Blood of Zapathasura it is in the core V5 book, on the p. 395, the Week of Nightmares loresheet as Lore 5<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T04:49:30-07:00","id":1511536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511501-antediluvian-blood-properties#post1511501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, as you probably know already, there are some stated &quot;miraculous&quot; effects of drinking the blood of some beings, among them, perhaps the Antediluvian ones are the most potent. As stated in books published, we only have Malkav's blood and Tremere's blood. Just for fun, giving that a single drop from Malkav's blood is stated to heal all wounds and derangements (save for the <i>permanent</i> one of the Malkavians), increase willpower by 1 and drop the generation by one, what do you guys think drinking the blood of each of the Antediluvians effect would be?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there should be this distinct possiblity and option to drink Vitae of a Founder ( or a Third Generation Vampire ) in circumstances or in a situation ( or during an event or an interaction ) where it is provided with permission and a definite choice by a Vampiress or a Vampire who is a Founder ( or, to give another category - a Sixth Generation Vampire Elder ) . In a situation with the stated qualities, the effects and benefits of the Vitae should be clearly different and unique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T08:02:03-07:00","id":1511540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511501-antediluvian-blood-properties?p=1511512#post1511512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Malkav's blood has the effects I mentioned in the text. A single drop heals all wounds and cures all derangements (except for the <b>permanent </b>one of Malkavians), drop generation by 1 and increases <i>permanent</i> Willpower by 1. It's in the story <b>Fountains of Bright Crimson</b>, not sure if you read this supplement for <b>Jerusalem by Night</b>. I was thinking about possible effects for other Antediluvians as a fun exercise, as the only one confirmed canonically is Malkav's (and Tremere's in a way).</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure this wasn't a rumor cited in the book, or that something else was done with that blood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T08:25:54-07:00","id":1511541,"title":"","content":"It is on page 32. in <b>Fountains of Bright Crimson</b>\u200b in Conclusions and Aftermath, where the book describes the possible outcomes, and the effects of this <i>very</i> potent prize...\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T09:27:19-07:00","id":1511544,"title":"","content":"As a side note, since Malkav's blood lowers your Generation, I think that should be a &quot;generic&quot; effect, at least based on BJD<br /> <br /> This part fits right in to that:<br /> <br /> <b>Ulwazi: </b>It appears that someone believes in God! I\u2019m an agnostic,myself. These \u201cScourges\u201d went out to exterminate weak vampires?<br /> <b>Beckett:</b> Yes.<br /> <b>Ulwazi: </b>Perhaps it worked! Nevertheless, this seems like a foolish solution. Why didn\u2019t you let them drink from the elders, to<br /> thicken young and thin ancient blood?<br /> <b>Beckett:</b> That\u2019s...a crime among us.<br /> <b>Sanaa:</b> They call it \u201cdiablerie.\u201d<br /> <b>Ulwazi:</b> I know, I know. We don\u2019t like it either.<br /> <b>Rilwan: </b>Xwetanu. They don\u2019t know those rituals. Ask yourself: How long have they hosted blood-drinkers in places like Europe and the Americas? 10,000 years? Five? It sounds impressive when you measure by Genesis, but we come from the beginning of all human time, and so do our vampires. Their elders don\u2019t know how to turn thin blood to thick, new to old and back again.<br /> <b>Sanaa:</b> I heard the Assamites\u200b learned if from Ethiopians, to concenrate their blood...<br /> <b>Rilwan: </b>Perhaps that can save them, but it is their values that are lacking. When elders refuse to give anything to their juniors, nothing can save them. When a father won\u2019t release his inheritance, his children starve, and he\u2019ll eventually look over a dusty field he\u2019s grown too old to till. Even immortals should fear this.<br /> <br /> I love this part in Beckett's Jyhad Diary; the idea of Elders have the ability to turn thin blood thick, lower ones generation and it is pure vampiric selfishness they refuse to do it, to keep the generation gap - basically saying the curse Caine laid on their children to behave, the introduction of the generation &quot;system&quot;, so the children will be always weaker than the Sire is... not even a curse, maybe the curse not even exist; it is just the natural effect of the embrace - before that every vampire were equal, the second and the third, wasn't any differenc, not even called &quot;generation&quot; back then. Caine? Caine is <i>not</i> a vampire. Not even died... <br /> Actually lots of the Clan's curses not even really come from Caine - well at least not according the Clan Books. Sure the generally accepted version is Caine gave out the curses, but then what about the Caitiff? They lack of any weakness... and basically their pre-conceptions about Vampires have a tendency to influence them somewhat. This not only influences strengths and weaknesses, but is the canon explanation for the disciplines they have when sired. If they believe vampires are &quot;supposed&quot; to be physically far superior to mortals, they'll start with Celerity, Potence, and Fortitude. If they believe Vampires Are Sex Gods, they'll start with Presence and/or Dominate. and so on. Or in the extreme cases, like the nosferatu, a nosferatu caitiff will be a very ugly one... but not a monster like its Sire. So the &quot;weakness&quot; is not necessarily inherent with the blood eg. the Curse fail to pass on sometimes. <br /> Sure, Caine done his fair share of cursing, but for example it is suggested it was Lilith who whispered a secret in Malkav's ear and that shattered his mind (even further and because of the twin-connecton, Malakai's too...) , Caine asked the Eldest to twist Absimilliard's flesh to reflect the inner monster, Saulot <i>ordered</i> his Clan to only accept blood as a gift and never take it with force (and Samiel further added to his Warriors to always help out someone in need) - and the antitribu twisted this to only the blood taken from an enemy or by force would satisfy them. Cappadocius' corpse like appearance came from the botched Emberace when the wraiths he pissed off tried to prevent it and managed to hold just enough of his soul back to have the corpse-like visage.Sutekh's curse came from Ra<br /> Anyhow, IF the generation could be lowered by a ritual (as this example highlighted, the Banu Haqim &quot;borrowed&quot; the technic from ethiopian Laibons) and with potent blood... and the Elders just not keen to make equals (or most of the cases even forgot how to do it) then the potent blood of the antediluvians should have that effect<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T09:37:41-07:00","id":1511545,"title":"","content":"I'd think drinking from the blood of an anti would create a vastly potent blood bound just from one taste instead of the typical three that would it take. Now I'm thinking that they could lower the generation of any kindred by sheer will into a more useful pawn. I.E. a 10th generation is now a 5th generation monster.<br /> <br /> Ventrue: Drinking from him I think you find your in clan disciplines are more effective and you gain insight in how to influence society to your liking. The downside is maybe your feeding requirements are more stringent.<br /> <br /> Brujah: Your intellectial curiosty is increased and your mental attributes and skills go up by one dot, but your more edgier then normal.<br /> <br /> Lasombra: Your profiency with Oblivion/Obteneration is enchanced and you gain a stronger assoication with the sea and gain some bonus at piloting a ship or building one. But you are more driven and ruthless to succeed with your plans.<br /> <br /> Malkavians: You have a stronger tie to the Network and gain more insight and clarity and thus your knowledge of Auspex is increased by a dot. But you are more likely to be overloaded by all the info your Auspex is feeding you.<br /> <br /> That's is all I can think of for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T11:18:48-07:00","id":1511554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are you sure this wasn't a rumor cited in the book, or that something else was done with that blood?\u200b </div> </div> </div>Naturally, I was sure when I made the post, in any case <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a> even answered for you, giving the page, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a side note, since Malkav's blood lowers your Generation, I think that should be a &quot;generic&quot; effect, at least based on BJD </div> </div> </div>I definitely agree. By the way there are some stories where it was said that this gap between generations didn't exist in the time of the Antediluvians and this is another satisfactory explanation and a very interesting &quot;quasi-Marxist&quot; one, by the way hahaha. There are a couple of powers that allow one to lower generation by drinking from a potion made with blood, etc. I guess <i>From Marduk's Throat</i> is likely the most famous, but there's also the <i>Pursuit of Apotheosis</i> in <b>Rites of Blood </b>(by the way a ritual that I think suits much more as from older and &quot;darker&quot; schools of blood sorcery than &quot;Anarch's crap&quot;, but that's another discussion lol) among others powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd think drinking from the blood of an anti would create a vastly potent blood bound just from one taste instead of the typical three that would it take. Now I'm thinking that they could lower the generation of any kindred by sheer will into a more useful pawn. I.E. a 10th generation is now a 5th generation monster.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>I definitely agree with that, by the way when considering these things that have the possibility of lowering one's generation, I always consider that if the one drinking has a very weak blood, he should drop more than one generation at once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T00:45:23-07:00","id":1511588,"title":"","content":"Another thing to consider, is until which generation could this work. Because, let's say, a Cainite of 4th Generation drinks from this blood, would it be reasonable for him to drop to the third generation? I'd normally say no, but it's a valid question nonetheless....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T05:54:29-07:00","id":1511606,"title":"","content":"I would say it work regardless of Genreration, becasue of two reason... well three<br /> First is the above reason from BJD - I know I sound like a broken old record^^<br /> The second is the bit logical aproach; it is easier to thicken an already strong vitae than a weak, &quot;diluted&quot; one; we even could see this in the diablerie and several generation lowering effects; farther you are from the source, the harder to reach it; Mithras was a 4th generation Methuselah\u200b, Montgomery Coven was a 11th Generation Child and after the deed, he not achived 4th Generation, only lowered to the 6th. Meanwhle, after the Baali Anaduk made a deal with a Demon who gifted Anaduk a succubus who could consume the Tablets of Ma-ri-ah and become the product of whatever was contained in them and since the tablets were incomplete, Ma-ri-ah was only partially recreated, full of disjointed and partial memories and corrupted by hate; she slew Anaduk upon waking and gorged on his blood, becoming a 7th Generation Baali in the process. After Mary the Black ate Michael, she became a 4th Generation Baali, not a 6th or 5th. Her blood was thicker.<br /> So by this logic, a 4th Generation could be easier to lower to 3 than a 6 for example. Some suplement even state something along the line, &quot;A vampire's vitae itself seek <i>perfection&quot; </i>and thats what urges the vampires to consume each other, to reach to source.<br /> Third is a bit blatant reasoning I know... but the description of Malkav's blood not mentions any generation limits; you drink it, you lower your generation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Would be logical, actually, the Antediluvians were Embraced before Generations became a thing, in a sense their vitae is a &quot;saved version&quot; what a Cainite blood should be like. Their progeny would be still a 4th Generation Child of course, but that is because of the nature of the Embrace; even their strong vitae is not capable to fully bridge the chasm between a Mortal and Immortal Blood God...<br /> ...but if you are basically a Blood God already?<br /> <br /> But lets face it, 98% of the time this question wouldn't even be asked, because it is really rare you face such a dileamma; only if you are already a ST for a player (or players) who <i>reached</i> the 4th Generation (or depending of your game, if they were Embraced in to it. Nahum ben Enosh was Embraced by Saulot in 216 CE, Gratiano de Veronese was Embraced in 1130 CE, Augustus Giovanni in 1005 CE, Jamal was a Caliph and Eldest of the Alamut until he died in 1998 with a bit more than eight centuries old, meaning this 4th generation Assamite was Embraced in the 12th century, so there quite a few example of 4th generations between 1000 and 2000 year old age), so worked their way up on the food chain<br /> Then I guess as a Storyteller I would say, let the player (or players) have it! Be a &quot;Teen-diluvian &quot;, to become a 3rd generation Cainite<br /> ...and face the consequences (because ooooh boy, there would be tons of it!) \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T07:07:01-07:00","id":1511610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511501-antediluvian-blood-properties?p=1511516#post1511516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The True Vessel was the semi-legendary recipient of the vitae and soul of the Cappadocian Antediluvian, which would enable Augustus Giovanni to complete the diablerie of his sire.<br /> Aside that, and Japeth used it to Embrace Agustus, the jar was filled with the vitae of Cappadocius for the Embrace ceremony (and Lamia cursed it with the painfull kiss)<br /> So the vitae left in it not only would allow Augustus to complete the diableire, but probably would have other funny properities.</div> </div> </div> </div>This might not be the case<br /> <br /> If you read clanbook cappadocian, pg 22, we get a Very in-depth look at how Giovanni was embraced, with Augustus's mortal blood being placed in what sounds suspiciously similar to the True Vessel. It is also notable that the people who have been in possession of the True Vessel have seemed to be curiously immune to the hostility of Clan Giovanni (Samedi) or had them embark on projects they would approve of (Setites).<br /> <br /> In addition, Japeth is the one that created and was the first to hold it, and also seems to have put the clan curse on the Giovanni.<br /> <br /> I believe the original intention was that the &quot;True Vessel&quot; was actually a trap designed for Augustus if he ever went rogue like the tremere. All it does it contain his Mortal blood, allowing any non-Giovanni who wields it a level of control over Augustus(and thus the Giovanni bloodline as a whole) and would have some horrible side effect if Augustus himself were to try to drink it(like say, turn him mortal).<br /> <br /> Granted, this is world of darkness. Even if all the writers were on board for this in 1997 when these supplements were being published, those writer have since changed and this would have probably been retconned anyway given the current direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T10:23:29-07:00","id":1511624,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m amending on Brujah slightly. If his intellectual side hIs dominate then your mental attributes go up by a dot but your more emotionally detached as a result. If it\u2019s Troile the passionate rebel then I think your social attributes go up by one dot but you are more short tempered.<br /> <br /> Set: I think a feeling of divinity would be expected and maybe a boost to resolve and composure rolls. Perhaps fellow Ministry members sense a profound change in you and treat you like one of his direct childer. Though with him in the afterlife I\u2019m not sure how that would work without major league possession of one his direct childer or grand childer to do the deed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 05-14-2023, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T11:04:10-07:00","id":1511629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would say it work regardless of Genreration, becasue of two reason... well three<br /> First is the above reason from BJD - I know I sound like a broken old record^^<br /> The second is the bit logical aproach; it is easier to thicken an already strong vitae than a weak, &quot;diluted&quot; one; we even could see this in the diablerie and several generation lowering effects; farther you are from the source, the harder to reach it; Mithras was a 4th generation Methuselah\u200b, Montgomery Coven was a 11th Generation Child and after the deed, he not achived 4th Generation, only lowered to the 6th. Meanwhle, after the Baali Anaduk made a deal with a Demon who gifted Anaduk a succubus who could consume the Tablets of Ma-ri-ah and become the product of whatever was contained in them and since the tablets were incomplete, Ma-ri-ah was only partially recreated, full of disjointed and partial memories and corrupted by hate; she slew Anaduk upon waking and gorged on his blood, becoming a 7th Generation Baali in the process. After Mary the Black ate Michael, she became a 4th Generation Baali, not a 6th or 5th. Her blood was thicker.<br /> So by this logic, a 4th Generation could be easier to lower to 3 than a 6 for example. Some suplement even state something along the line, &quot;A vampire's vitae itself seek <i>perfection&quot; </i>and thats what urges the vampires to consume each other, to reach to source.\u200b </div> </div> </div>It's a good argument, I must say, regarding Montgomery and Mary the Black, specially. I remember when I first read about Montgomery I thought with myself that it was too obvious who was in charge there lol, I only felt sorry for Mithras for having to deal being a 6th generation vampire with a much weakened character sheet (even though Mithras original character sheet didn't make him justice in the first place and I always changed it, but at least it was better than Montgomery-Mithras one. Mary the Black has a fascinating story, I just always wondered how on earth (or better in this case, on Hell lol) wasn't Michael able to easily control her after the deed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Third is a bit blatant reasoning I know... but the description of Malkav's blood not mentions any generation limits; you drink it, you lower your generation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Would be logical, actually, the Antediluvians were Embraced before Generations became a thing, in a sense their vitae is a &quot;saved version&quot; what a Cainite blood should be like. Their progeny would be still a 4th Generation Child of course, but that is because of the nature of the Embrace; even their strong vitae is not capable to fully bridge the chasm between a Mortal and Immortal Blood God...<br /> ...but if you are basically a Blood God already?\u200b </div> </div> </div>This reason is probably enough in itself, I'd say, my main concern isn't even PCs of 4th Generation (as I'm yet to have one in 20+ years of experience as a Storyteller), but more to the scenario really and antagonists. After my group of PCs helped my game's antagonist acquire the <i>Sargon Fragment </i>(and perform the Ritual of Apotheosis, yes they even protected him while he made the ritual and other NPCs were trying to &quot;save the world&quot; and stop him lol), this kind of thing really worries me, because giving too much power to certain characters in a story could be a good way to basically end the story lol. In any case, your reasons are good and I have to agree with them. Regarding players dropping their generation and having to deal with the consequences, that's also something I always tell my players, <b>beware</b> hahaha...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Be a &quot;Teen-diluvian &quot; </div> </div> </div>This is a really gunny term, I'm gonna use it from now hahaha","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T11:54:56-07:00","id":1511635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511501-antediluvian-blood-properties?p=1511629#post1511629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mary the Black has a fascinating story, I just always wondered how on earth (or better in this case, on Hell lol) wasn't Michael able to easily control her after the deed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Love<br /> In Constantinople by Night it is described, she consumed Him, she gained parts of his memories, learning that he never intended to leave her and that the only reason she had succeeded in killing him was because he had allowed it and till the bitter end, he loved Her. - this drove her to frenzy<br /> <br /> In V20 goes a bit deeper (BJD again)<br /> Mary the Black and Michael the Patriarch became one after she diablerized him to complete her vengeance. But, in so doing, she cursed herself with the burden of knowledge and a truth that scourged her soul. Her revenge was empty, for the man she loathed to the depths of her being had not abandoned her of his own will, but had been forced from her side and had never, in his heart of hearts, ceased to love her. In the depths of her own grief and madness, she sought death to blot out this knowledge... but instead, in the deep places of her own being, she found what was left of him, and together they became more than they could ever become alone. Istanbul remains a shining beacon of mortal faith above, a city sacred to many; now, below, in the remains of Michael\u2019s long-abandoned haven, Mary the Black forges a Well of Sacrifice that will make its underbelly a perfect reflection of hell on Earth, as well. She intends to make Constantinople a literal gateway to Hell, recruiting to her side the Carthaginian Assamite Eshmunazar, and reaching out to Dylan Bruce to become the third party. She intends for the ancient Eshmunazar to act as darkness, while she and Michael play the role of balance. Dylan Bruce is to become Lucifer\u2019s light, before plunging the entire city \u2014 and possibly the world \u2014 into Hell. Michael is conscious inside the form of Mary, waiting and watching as he subtly pushes her, attempting to exert his will over her body.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511501-antediluvian-blood-properties?p=1511629#post1511629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a really gunny term, I'm gonna use it from now hahaha</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> *Duing the best Palpatine impression* <br /> Do it ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T12:29:57-07:00","id":1511639,"title":"","content":"Michael always scheming even from the grave.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T21:50:18-07:00","id":1511691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Love<br /> In Constantinople by Night it is described, she consumed Him, she gained parts of his memories, learning that he never intended to leave her and that the only reason she had succeeded in killing him was because he had allowed it and till the bitter end, he loved Her. - this drove her to frenzy\u200b </div> </div> </div>This I know, I have Constantinople by Night (a wonderful book btw) on my computer desk right now by the way, but that was before even the idea that a diablerized Cainite could dominate the one diablerizing him was even a thing. I read this book when I was a child and at the time I remember I was angry because he allowed himself to be destroyed (as I mentioned, at the time this notion of a canite dominating the diablerist wasn't even a thing) because I quite liked the character, not because of the reason itself, as love is surely enough to drive one to do this kind of thing, especially when coupled with guilt. Later, after the new vision of diablerie came (at Transylvania Chronicles with the idea of Saulot using Tremere, etc) I began to wonder how did she manage to overcome his will.<br /> <br /> I know BJD addresses that (quite well, by the way), even though for me, it's hard to see Eshmunazar taking part in it, Dylan Bruce sure, as he seem to be up for anything that might cause trouble for the world lol, but I've always had a quite different vision of Eshmunazar, it's hard to see him banding together with Mary <i>the Black</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T15:23:34-07:00","id":1511827,"title":"","content":"They say politics make for strange bedfellows and I think on how Mary the Black is an meth herself could be a factor of finding enough willpower to fight off the effects of Michael's control or maybe there is other factors at play that we are unaware off considering she was already a long dead ghoul when she was brought back by the Baali and there strange masters they serve..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T18:23:33-07:00","id":1511947,"title":"","content":"I thought I had read somewhere that Mary the Black had become a demon, having transcended the vampiric curse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T21:08:58-07:00","id":1511966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511501-antediluvian-blood-properties?p=1511947#post1511947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought I had read somewhere that Mary the Black had become a demon, having transcended the vampiric curse?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm not mistaken it was in Constantinople by Night itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T08:38:10-07:00","id":1512014,"title":"","content":"Not to mention in the clan book of the Baali there is talk that she has becoming akin to blood goddess and no mere cainite and Constantinople by Night details it was a ritual that brought forth some sort of succubus that would become the thing that was transcribed on the tablets written by Mariah. Like I said her origins of how she became a vampire is unique compared to the rest of her fellow undead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 05-18-2023, 04:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T08:49:25-07:00","id":1512018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511501-antediluvian-blood-properties?p=1511544#post1511544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a side note, since Malkav's blood lowers your Generation, I think that should be a &quot;generic&quot; effect, at least based on BJD<br /> <br /> This part fits right in to that:<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the context for this conversation? Seems needlessly and specifically anti-white given that the middle east and Indian cities operate virtually the same as their western counterparts and yet get excluded from any criticism.(well, what I thought was Assamite effort to develop an incredible ritual is now just something they stole, so screw them too right?) US writers really aught to stop pushing their racist attitudes on the rest of the world. /rant<br /> <br /> <br /> On topic<br /> As I imagine things, vampires slowly build up their attributes and disciplines through feeding, and accumulate power which can be bestowed to ghouls to raise their attributes/disciplines. They're siphoning away wealth from the masses as parasites and redistributing it to a chosen few (ghouls/childer). Antedeluvians have been siphoning away wealth into their ultra-concentrated blood for millennia, their blood so rich and their attributes so exaggerated that a single drop is worth years of ordinary feeding. <br /> <br /> Also, In older books, elder blood could raise a drinker's disciplines temporarily. As I rule this, one dot for every level beyond 5th is given to the drinker provided the new level doesn't exceed the donors. So if you have 4 Potence and you drink from someone with 8 potence, you temporarily have 7 potence. But if you had 7 Auspex and drank the blood of someone with 8 Auspex you will only go up to 8 Auspex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T09:24:35-07:00","id":1512021,"title":"","content":"The idea of Elders (or basically any vempire really with sufficiently low generation) have/had the ability to turn thin blood thick, lower ones generation and it is pure vampiric selfishness they refuse to do it, to keep the generation gap with their vitae and a ritual - to the point they even forgot, never passed down the knowledge to their youngs and became basically bloated ticks (and a side effect, since they not &quot;refreshed their anceint blood became the victims of the &quot;Thirst of Caine&quot; and human blood wont sustain them)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T13:25:33-07:00","id":1512043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511501-antediluvian-blood-properties?p=1512021#post1512021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of Elders (or basically any vempire really with sufficiently low generation) have/had the ability to turn thin blood thick, lower ones generation and it is pure vampiric selfishness they refuse to do it, to keep the generation gap with their vitae and a ritual - to the point they even forgot, never passed down the knowledge to their youngs and became basically bloated ticks (and a side effect, since they not &quot;refreshed their anceint blood became the victims of the &quot;Thirst of Caine&quot; and human blood wont sustain them)</div> </div> </div> </div>What a sick way to continue there endless cycle of betrayal &amp; warfare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T18:37:48-07:00","id":1512395,"title":"","content":"Depends if I'm running cannon 3rd-gen. For one, each blood-point is worth two: I'd exaggerate the clan-weakness; Brujah, roll for frenzy. Venture; Blood bound to all Venture, one drink. In return, they also get a dot, one time only, in the clan's discipline. Yeah, you drink from Lord Nos himself and lose a point of appearance, but you gain a dot in Obfuscate, even if that dot brings it to a level-six; what's a level-six to an antediluvian?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T00:03:37-07:00","id":1512407,"title":"","content":"In a chronicle I was running the coterie came across 3 vials of Ravnos vitae. Each vial lowered the drinker's gen by 1 and made them experience various memories of the antediluvian. When they woke up they were then part of a highlander-sque plot where everyone who had drank the vitae was compelled to hunt and diablerize others who had drunken the vitae in order to awaken it and allow a 4 gen to become the new Ravnos antediluvian. Culver City was quickly becoming a hot zone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T05:24:42-07:00","id":1512429,"title":"","content":"What book talks about Tremere's blood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T06:26:13-07:00","id":1512442,"title":"","content":"House of Tremere describes the details of the Ritual of Usurpation and whats happened after<br /> But details about Tremere's own blood?<br /> Not much<br /> More so, Tremere have only one canonical Progeny, Grimgroth<br /> Later editions expanded a bit the ritual and the stolen blood, the vicissitude posioning and the flaw to have a 3rd eye<br /> And why a Baali could pass as a Tremere under a ritual...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T06:48:09-07:00","id":1512445,"title":"","content":"Unrelated question but I don't want to open a topic just for a detail.<br /> Does any kind of time-travel magic exists in the world of darkness?<br /> <br /> Aaaaand...<br /> has anybody used that to visit ancient Ur, Enoch, or to meet the antediluvians?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 05-23-2023, 09:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T07:06:04-07:00","id":1512448,"title":"","content":"Aside from a whole discipline called Temporis? Especially the Discipline powers of:<br /> <b>Rewind Time:</b> Move up to a day backwards in time (Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand)<br /> <b>Pocket Out of Time:</b> Shift an entire area outside of time (Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand)<br /> <b>Domain of Evernight:</b> Dilate time so that day passes in a blink of an eye (Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand)<br /> <b>Cheat the Fates: </b>Reflexively step outside of time for several rounds (Players Guide to High Clans)<br /> <b>Insight: </b>Step forward in time to see how your next actions are going to turn out (Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand)<br /> <b>Quicksilver Contemplation</b>: Stop time around you in order to consider the best possible next move. - Auspex 2 Temporis 3 combination discipline (Players Guide to High Clans)<br /> <br /> <b>Time</b> is one of nine Spheres of magic in Mage<br /> Mages studying Time magic agree that the world is full of unexpected whorls and vortices of temporal disturbance. Time contracts around some places and dilates at others, though the regimentation of scientific time means that such phenomena are not as common as they once were. In unusual circumstances, time may loop back on itself, make jumps and rifts to past or future, or diverge in multiple streams.<br /> You can find the powers in Mage: The Ascension Revised Edition and Masters of the Art<br /> <br /> <b>The Lore of Patterns </b>allows a Neberu to manipulate time in ways both subtle, such as causing apparent serendipity, to outright slowing or stopping the time flow. They can also read the patterns of the heavens, telling the future and enabling them to alter it.<br /> It is in the Demon: The Fallen Rulebook<br /> <br /> Aside that, Demons in general (not the Fallen) or Djins or any other entity depends of the storyteller's taste could grant &quot;wishes&quot; - with trime travel for exmaple<br /> I think even Changeling: The Dreaming have some Art that manipulates time and/or cause and effect<br /> And it is not out of the realm of possibility the Weaver-tech or potent Weaver-spirit could make a Time-gate, if the Patern and sicience allows it (latest studies show, yes, possible)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 05-23-2023, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T07:12:00-07:00","id":1512449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511501-antediluvian-blood-properties?p=1512445#post1512445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">has anybody used that to visit ancient Ur, Enoch, or to meet the antediluvians?</div> </div> </div> </div>No<br /> But had plenty of games where the palyers started in the First City and were proto-antedulivans themselves or their children<br /> And other historical games in anctient times, Baali Wars, Siege of Ur by the Settites, etc<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T10:45:08-07:00","id":1512472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511501-antediluvian-blood-properties?p=1512445#post1512445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unrelated question but I don't want to open a topic just for a detail.<br /> Does any kind of time-travel magic exists in the world of darkness?<br /> <br /> The True Brujah line has a disciplines that gives them control over aspects of time and the other posters will give you plenty of examples of that ability.<br /> Aaaaand...<br /> has anybody used that to visit ancient Ur, Enoch, or to meet the antediluvians?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as far as I know and I heard or read somewhere that the True Brujah tried to go back in time to meet there progenitor or even try to change things and found that something is preventing them from doing such a thing. It's was the same thing in Mage The Awakening 1st edition that masters of the time arcana couldn't find away to see Atlantis or travel to that period of time as it was thought that perhaps that the Exarchs did something to world.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T20:07:43-07:00","id":1512532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511501-antediluvian-blood-properties?p=1512445#post1512445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unrelated question but I don't want to open a topic just for a detail.<br /> Does any kind of time-travel magic exists in the world of darkness?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Revised edition book <i>Blood Sacrifice: The Thaumaturgy Companion</i> detailed a Dur-an-ki ritual that could send people's consciousness back in time to possess the bodies of mortals participating in certain Mithraic ceremonies in the distant past.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}